  "player_hint_1_en": "Only one square fits Henry's clue (\"He was beside a column and the statue.\"). So Henry (H) must be at row 2, column 5. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_2_en": "With the rows and columns of Henry crossed out, only one square is left for Dante that fits his clue (\"He was beside the chest.\"). So Dante (D) must be at row 1, column 9. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_3_en": "Suppose Amber were at row 4, column 7: then nobody could stand in row 8. So Amber can't be there. Suppose Grace were at row 6, column 2: then Vaughn would have nowhere left to go. So Grace can't be there. Testing the remaining squares the same way rules out a few more. So Amber (A) must be at row 4, column 8. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_4_en": "Suppose Floyd were at row 5, column 4: then Vaughn would have nowhere left to go. So Floyd can't be there. Suppose Elsa were at row 5, column 6: then Floyd would have nowhere left to go. So Elsa can't be there. Testing the remaining squares the same way rules out a few more. That leaves only one possible square for Barnaby that fits his clue (\"He was beside a box.\"). Barnaby is now the only person who can still go in row 8. So Barnaby (B) must be at row 8, column 7. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_5_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Clement that fits his clue (\"He was in the Workshop or the Lobby.\"). So Clement (C) must be at row 9, column 4. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_6_en": "Elsa is now the only person who can still go in column 6. So Elsa (E) must be at row 6, column 6. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_7_en": "Using the general clue (\"There was exactly one person beside a shelf.\"), some squares are ruled out for Grace. So Grace (G) must be at row 7, column 1. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_8_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Floyd that fits his clue (\"He was not on a carpet. He was exactly two rows north of Grace.\"). So Floyd (F) must be at row 5, column 2. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_9_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Vaughn. So Vaughn (the victim) must be at row 3, column 3. Cross out his row and column. Floyd is the only person in the Painting Gallery with Vaughn, so Floyd is the murderer!"
 },
